Sentiment Analysis on Amazon Baby Product Reviews
This project implements a sentiment analysis model to classify Amazon Baby Product reviews into positive, negative, and neutral categories. The dataset consists of user reviews with star ratings, and the goal is to predict sentiment based on the text of each review.

Project Overview
The analysis uses machine learning algorithms to process product reviews and predict the sentiment behind each review. Specifically, the project utilizes a Logistic Regression model trained on a text dataset and evaluates its performance using metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.

Dataset
The dataset used in this project is from Amazon reviews for baby products. Each review contains a text field and a rating field (1 to 5 stars). 
The data is preprocessed to classify reviews as follows:
Positive: Ratings 4 and 5
Negative: Ratings 1 and 2
Neutral: Ratings 3
Steps Involved:
Data Loading:
The dataset is loaded from Google Drive and prepared for analysis.

Data Preprocessing:
Text data is cleaned and vectorized using CountVectorizer, converting reviews into numerical features for the model.
Model Training:
A Logistic Regression model is trained to classify reviews based on sentiment.

Model Evaluation:
The model is evaluated on a test set, with performance metrics reported, including accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.

Technologies Used:
Python
Pandas, NumPy
Scikit-learn
Google Colab

How to Run the Project:
Clone this repository to your local machine.
Install required dependencies using pip install -r requirements.txt.
Run the sentiment_analysis.py script to train the model and evaluate it.


